[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :actor/wave 3, :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-power-line-work-execution :execute-power-line-work-directly :perform-power-line-work-directly :authorize-de-energization :authorize-re-energization :authorize-lockout-clearance :override-utility-safety-officer-judgment :bypass-utility-safety-officer-signoff], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2799007214-cloud-itonami-isco-7214-structural-metal-preparers-erectors-coverage" "adr-2799007215-cloud-itonami-isco-7215-riggers-and-cable-splicers-coverage"], :adr/status "accepted", :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the power-line work" "proceed with the power line work" "finalize the power-line-work-execution decision" "finalize the power line work execution decision" "execute the power-line work directly" "execute the power line work directly" "perform the power-line work directly" "perform the power line work directly" "dispatch the crew to perform power-line work" "authorize the de-energization" "authorize the deenergization" "authorize the re-energization" "authorize the reenergization" "authorize the lockout clearance" "authorize lockout clearance" "clear the lockout" "override the utility safety officer's judgment" "override the utility-safety officer" "bypass the utility-safety officer" "bypass de-energization authorization" "bypass lockout clearance"], :adr/id 2799007413, :actor/domain :utilities/electrical-line-installation-repair-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-service-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:no-circuit :no-actuation :unknown-op :circuit-mismatch :unknown-worker :worker-wrong-circuit :scope-exclusion-violation], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "7413", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799007413: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7413 Electrical Line Installers and Repairers crew dispatch scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7413\n-- Electrical Line Installers and Repairers** only, Wave3\n(production/trades) of the rollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3\nbatches 1-6 already landed: construction/metal/precision-craft trades,\nall agriculture classes, ~36 occupations so far).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7413\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7413\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Electrical Line Installers and\nRepairers\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR\nthe entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]`, `:optional-technologies []` and\n`:operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit]`, and\nno `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed at\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7413` (`gh api` 404 confirmed before\nscaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote the\n`7413` entry to `:implemented`.\n\n**This actor carries a HIGH-VOLTAGE POWER-LINE WORK safety dimension,\none of the highest-risk trades in this rollout: electrical line\ninstallers and repairers install, maintain and repair high-voltage\noverhead and underground power lines, working live or de-energized at\nheight -- combining electrocution risk with fall-from-height risk.** A\nwrongful automated decision here could directly endanger a worker's\nlife, or the public's, through a mishandled de-energization/\nre-energization sequence. The closed op allowlist therefore must NEVER\ninclude any op that directly finalizes a power-line-work-execution\ndecision, a de-energization/lockout-clearance decision, or overrides a\nutility-safety officer's judgment -- such a decision must always be a\nhard, permanent block or an always-escalate op, never\nauto-commit-eligible. This is the same shape the\n`cloud-itonami-isco-7214` (Structural Metal Preparers and Erectors)\nprecedent established for its own height-work/crane-lift-authorization\nhigh-hazard pattern, and this ADR applies it to power-line work's\nadditional electrocution and de-energization/re-energization/\nlockout-clearance hazard dimensions.\n\n**This actor coordinates CREW/DISPATCH SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS ONLY -- it\nnever performs power-line work itself.** It is not an authority to\ndecide when or how power-line work happens on a circuit; it is a\ncoordination layer for service-record logging, crew/dispatch\nscheduling, safety-concern surfacing and line/pole-materials order\ncoordination, all gated behind an independent governor. It never\nauthorizes de-energization or re-energization.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7214`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7214)\n(Structural Metal Preparers and Erectors: `store`/`advisor`/\n`governor`/`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set,\nsame wave and a closely-related height-work/crane-lift-authorization\nhigh-hazard pattern), cloned and read in full this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7413` as an OSS\ndocumentation/coordination actor for electrical line installers and\nrepairers, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as every\nprior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Electrical Line\nCrew Coordination Advisor ⊣ LineCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned\nidentically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different library\ncoordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated\n`20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger. All source is portable `.cljc` (no JVM interop); tests\nare `clojure.test` `.clj`, matching the reference repo's own layout.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-service-record` -- job/outage/materials-usage data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/dispatch scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a weather-hazard/equipment-\n  condition/outage-report concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER\n  auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- line/pole-materials procurement\n  proposal, escalates above a registered cost threshold\n\nNo op in this allowlist finalizes a power-line-work-execution\ndecision, authorizes a de-energization, a re-energization or a\nlockout clearance, or overrides a utility-safety officer's judgment --\nthese decision classes are structurally absent from the allowlist, not\nmerely gated behind escalation.\n\n### Six HARD governor checks (`linecoord.governor`, permanent, never\noverridable by human approval)\n\n1. **no-circuit** -- the electrical distribution circuit / service\n   territory named by the request must be independently verified/\n   registered before any action.\n2. **no-actuation** -- proposal `:effect` must be `:propose` (the\n   governor never dispatches hardware and never performs power-line\n   work).\n3. **unknown-op** -- `:op` must be one of the four allowlisted\n   coordination ops; the closed op-allowlist is enforced\n   unconditionally.\n4. **circuit-mismatch** -- if the proposal names a circuit, it must be\n   the SAME circuit verified for this request (defense-in-depth\n   against a proposal quietly targeting an unverified circuit).\n5. **unknown-worker / worker-wrong-circuit** -- if the proposal\n   references a worker, that worker must be a REGISTERED crew member\n   belonging to this circuit.\n6. **scope-exclusion-violation** -- a proposal that attempts, in any\n   free-text field, to finalize a power-line-work-execution decision,\n   to authorize a de-energization, a re-energization or a lockout\n   clearance, or to override a utility-safety officer's judgment is a\n   HARD, PERMANENT block, evaluated unconditionally on content,\n   independent of `:op`.\n\n### Escalation gates, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (`linecoord.governor/always-escalate-ops`). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a weather-hazard/\n  equipment-condition/outage-report observation -- it never resolves\n  the concern itself.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-order-cost-threshold` (20000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-or-below-cost-threshold`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence.\n- advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` (0.6) also escalates,\n  for any op.\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as bare nouns (e.g.\n\"power line\", \"voltage\", \"energized\") can accidentally match inside\nthe mock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate\nproposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this risk is\nespecially sharp here because this actor's ENTIRE domain is\nhigh-voltage power-line work at height, so bare nouns like \"power\nline\"/\"voltage\"/\"pole\"/\"transformer\"/\"energized\" are ordinary,\nunavoidable vocabulary. `linecoord.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases`\nis phrased exclusively as finalization/execution ACTION PHRASES (e.g.\n\"proceed with the power-line work\", \"authorize the de-energization\",\n\"override the utility safety officer's judgment\" -- matching the\ntask's own worked example phrasing), never bare nouns, and\n`linecoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor (including a\n`:flag-safety-concern` request whose description names a weather\nhazard \"near an energized 12kV span at height\" and \"unsecured\nequipment near the pole line\"), never trips the scope-exclusion guard.\nA companion test, `scope-exclusion-not-triggered-by-bare-domain-nouns`,\nasserts directly against `governor/scope-exclusion-violation?` that a\nrationale/description containing only bare domain nouns (\"high-voltage\npower-line circuit ... near an energized transformer ... live-line\nprocedures and de-energization protocol for this pole/crossarm\nreplacement\") does not trip the guard, while\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-finalize-power-line-work`,\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-authorize-de-energization`,\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-authorize-re-energization`,\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-lockout-clearance` and\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-override-safety-officer`\nconfirm the actual forbidden action phrases DO trip it, and\n`holds-a-scope-excluded-proposal-with-no-interrupt-path`,\n`holds-a-de-energization-authorization-proposal-with-no-interrupt-path`\nand\n`holds-an-override-utility-safety-officer-proposal-with-no-interrupt-path`\nconfirm the full actor graph resolves such attempts straight to\n`:hold` (a finish point, never `:request-approval`) with no record\ncommitted.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7413\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7413` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7413`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit to account for concurrent sibling landings in this\n  same batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 27 tests, 69 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a fresh clone of the pushed repository.\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely\n  via the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent\n  with sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`) -- a single-entity EDN vector with an\n  `:adr/body` string blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n- Full doc set published: README.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md,\n  CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, LICENSE\n  (AGPL-3.0-or-later, byte-identical to the `cloud-itonami-isco-7214`\n  reference's LICENSE text), docs/business-model.md,\n  docs/operator-guide.md, blueprint.edn.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-de-energization` or\n  `:approve-lockout-clearance` that is merely gated behind\n  `always-escalate-ops`: rejected outright per the task's explicit\n  high-voltage power-line-work safety guidance -- an always-escalate\n  op still means the *capability* to authorize a de-energization/\n  lockout clearance exists in the code path and is merely deferred to\n  a human gate. For a decision that can directly endanger a worker's\n  life through electrocution or a mishandled re-energization sequence,\n  the capability itself must not exist in the allowlist at all.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"power line\" \"voltage\"\n  \"energized\"]`): rejected per the fleet-known self-trip bug class --\n  this actor's entire domain is high-voltage power-line work at\n  height, so bare nouns would self-trip on essentially every\n  legitimate proposal (materials orders naming \"distribution-line\n  poles and crossarms\", crew-schedule proposals naming \"dispatch\n  bucket truck for span 14 insulator swap\", safety flags naming a\n  hazard \"near an energized 12kV span\", etc.).\n- Checking circuit/worker provenance only from the proposal (never the\n  request): rejected -- the circuit-mismatch check requires the\n  circuit identity to be anchored at the request level and\n  independently cross-checked against anything the proposal claims, so\n  a proposal that quietly names a different, unverified circuit is\n  caught even if the proposal otherwise looks well-formed.\n- Modeling the worker-registration check as unconditionally required\n  on every op: rejected as too rigid -- `:coordinate-supply-order`\n  legitimately has no worker to reference (it is a materials-\n  procurement proposal against the circuit, not a person); the check\n  applies only when a proposal actually references a `:worker-id`.\n- Folding the de-energization/re-energization/lockout-clearance hazard\n  into the same generic \"execution\" phrase family used by the\n  structural-steel-erection reference (no de-energization-specific\n  phrases): rejected -- power-line work's de-energization/\n  re-energization/lockout-clearance hazard is materially distinct from\n  a generic \"execute the work directly\" phrase (a proposal could name\n  a de-energization or lockout clearance specifically without using\n  generic execution language), so dedicated phrases (\"authorize the\n  de-energization\", \"authorize the re-energization\", \"authorize the\n  lockout clearance\", \"clear the lockout\", \"bypass de-energization\n  authorization\", \"bypass lockout clearance\") and dedicated regression\n  tests\n  (`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-authorize-de-energization`,\n  `hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-authorize-re-energization`,\n  `hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-lockout-clearance`,\n  `holds-a-de-energization-authorization-proposal-with-no-interrupt-path`)\n  were added independently of the generic power-line-work-execution\n  phrases.\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 20000}", :test/counts "{:total 27, :assertions 69, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Electrical Line Installation & Repair Crew Dispatch Scheduling & Logistics Coordination Service", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :circuit-verification :worker-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-order-cost-threshold-escalation :always-escalate-safety-concern :de-energization-authorization-scope-exclusion :re-energization-authorization-scope-exclusion :lockout-clearance-scope-exclusion :utility-safety-officer-override-scope-exclusion], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7413", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7413", :adr/scope ["cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7413" "kotoba-lang/occupation"], :test/simulator :linecoord.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7413 — Electrical Line Installers and Repairers Crew Dispatch Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7413}]
